# LIMS UI forms (React / Inertia)

These rules apply to **screens users fill in the browser**, not controlled PDF overlays.

## Composition

- **Sections:** `@/components/intake/form-section` — title + optional description, `border-t` dividers (`first` skips top rule).
- **Extract** repeated step UI (package rows, summaries) to `@/components/intake/*` with props only — no duplicated submit logic.
- **Labels:** `@/components/ui/label` + `htmlFor`; inputs from `@/components/ui/input`, `textarea`, `checkbox`.

## Validation UX

- Mirror server rules in client `canContinue` / step guards; set `attemptedContinue` when user hits Next on invalid step.
- Optional fields: omit required asterisk; allow empty string in payload when backend marks `nullable`.
- Payment/classification conditional blocks: show dependent fields only when parent value matches (see intake wizard step 2).

## Data integrity (intake tests step)

- Do not change **`estimatedTotal`** formula or package toggle semantics unless product owner requests it.
- Summary UI may **group** package vs individual lines for display only; persistence stays `selectedTypes` / package ids as today.

## Admin CRUD forms

- Follow existing admin pages under `resources/js/pages/admin/` (tables, dialogs, Inertia `router.post/put/delete`).
- Catalog edits (analysis types, packages) must stay consistent with `catalog_scope`, aqua visibility flags, and package `analysis_type_ids`.

## Accessibility

- Accordion/category toggles: `aria-expanded` on trigger buttons.
- Errors: visible text + `role="alert"` for step-level messages.
